      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name} You're correct, I can make a converter Input Field (or something like \"How about this URL: *url*\"), for convinence. The one I want it to be fixed is to allow redirections of 'known' URLs, such as youtu.be -> youtube.com patterns.\n\nThis is pretty good idea to minimize the user hassle. But I think it's easily solvable by VRC allowing at least one redirection for trusted (or even separated list of redirection allowed) URLs.\n\nI know this is pretty much optional and both youtu.be and youtube.com/watch?v= works just fine with yt-dlp (it just parses ID from URL and does its thing), but I think this (at least) 1 allowed redirection of trusted URLs might be helpful for some creators, including me and many more in future.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
